\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Heuristic oracle advantage at $\lambda =0.8$. The benchmark row uses the 14 chains with at least four tiers and at most 350 nodes (7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 24), three overlays each, 16 seeded evaluations per instance; the deeper, smaller chains are those in which latent structure has something to hide. Table~\ref {tab:lam0} covers all 32 retained chains at 10 seeded evaluations per instance, and the sweep of Section~\ref {sec:sweep} uses 8. All three counts are taken from the archived result files. Seeds are nested within instances, and the instance is the unit of analysis throughout (Section~\ref {sec:units}).}}{23}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
